3. Red Hat Official Images — Via JFrog Proxy
No custom build needed. Red Hat maintains security patches. JFrog proxies the pull.

3a. Single-Tool Red Hat Images (direct replacement for retired custom images)
Image	JFrog Proxy URL	Source Registry	Replaces	Used In
hi/git:2.54.0	...-docker-virtual/hi/git:2.54.0	registry.access.redhat.com	epay-ci-base (for git jobs)	version, tag, back-merge, values.update
ubi9/podman:9.7-1778086050	...-docker-virtual/ubi9/podman:9.7-1778086050	registry.access.redhat.com	epay-podman (retired)	image-build, image-push, image-retag
rhtas/cosign-rhel9:1.3.4-1776330019	...-docker-virtual/rhtas/cosign-rhel9:1.3.4-1776330019	registry.redhat.io ⚠️	epay-cosign (retired)	image-sign, image-sbom-attest
rhacs-roxctl-rhel8:4.10.2-1	...-docker-virtual/advanced-cluster-security/rhacs-roxctl-rhel8:4.10.2-1	registry.redhat.io ⚠️	epay-roxctl (retired)	image-scan:rhacs
⚠️ registry.redhat.io requires Red Hat subscription credentials.
JFrog admin must configure the virtual repo remote with RHN username/token.
Alternatively: mirror once with skopeo (see Air-Gap Build Process).

Why use Red Hat official instead of custom:

Security-patched by Red Hat with OCP certified images
FIPS-compliant out of the box
No custom Dockerfile maintenance
Version updates = change one image tag line in job YAML
