5. App Runtime Base Images Per Language
Runtime images are injected at image:build time via BASE_IMAGE ARG in each app Dockerfile.
Controlled per-tier by BASE_IMAGE_DEV_ENV and BASE_IMAGE_HIGHER_ENV variables in orchestrators.

artifactory.jfrog.sbi:443/itepaypg-sbiepay2-docker-virtual/ubi9/<runtime-image>:<tag>
Language	Build/Test Image	Runtime (App Dockerfile BASE_IMAGE)	Separated?	Orchestrator
Java	ubi9/openjdk-21 (JDK)	ubi9/openjdk-21-runtime (JRE only)	✅ Yes — compiler removed	templates/ci/backend/java.yml
.NET	ubi9/dotnet-80 (SDK)	ubi9/dotnet-80-runtime (runtime only)	✅ Yes — Roslyn compiler removed	templates/ci/backend/dotnet.yml
React/Angular	ubi9/nodejs-20 (full)	ubi9/nginx-124 (nginx only)	✅ Yes — Node.js not needed at runtime	templates/ci/frontend/react.yml
Node.js	ubi9/nodejs-20 (full — npm needed)	ubi9/nodejs-20-minimal (node binary only)	✅ Yes — npm/yarn removed from runtime	templates/ci/backend/nodejs.yml
Python	ubi9/python-39 (full — pip needed)	ubi9/python-39 (full — same image)	❌ No — pip runs inside Dockerfile RUN	templates/ci/backend/python.yml
PHP	ubi9/php-82 (full)	ubi9/php-82 (full — same image)	❌ No — no minimal variant exists	templates/ci/backend/php.yml
Variables in each orchestrator template (example — nodejs.yml):

variables:
  BASE_IMAGE_DEV_ENV:    "artifactory.jfrog.sbi:443/itepaypg-sbiepay2-docker-virtual/ubi9/nodejs-20:1-38"
  BASE_IMAGE_HIGHER_ENV: "artifactory.jfrog.sbi:443/itepaypg-sbiepay2-docker-virtual/ubi9/nodejs-20:1-38"
image:build selects tier:

case "$CI_COMMIT_BRANCH" in
  release/* | hotfix/* | main) BASE_IMAGE="$BASE_IMAGE_HIGHER_ENV" ;;
  *)                           BASE_IMAGE="$BASE_IMAGE_DEV_ENV"    ;;
esac
podman build --build-arg BASE_IMAGE="$BASE_IMAGE" ...
Why Python and PHP cannot use minimal runtime images:

Python:
  pip install runs INSIDE the app Dockerfile RUN step at image:build time.
  The runtime image must have pip to install packages into the container.
  python-39-minimal has no pip — Dockerfile build fails.
  To use minimal: would need to pre-vendor all deps in CI build stage and
  COPY vendor folder into minimal image — different deployment model, future option.

PHP:
  No php-82-minimal exists in Red Hat UBI.
  PHP runtime inherently includes the interpreter — no JRE/JDK-style split.

Node.js — why minimal works:
  npm is only needed to compile (npm ci, npm run build) — done in CI build stage.
  At runtime, pod runs: node /app/server.js — node binary only.
  nodejs-20-minimal has node binary but no npm/yarn — exactly what runtime needs.
  Build/test stages (nodejs.yml, nodejs.unit.yml) still use nodejs-20 (full).
